Installing and Running the Portable Agena Win64 Version
-------------------------------------------------------

If you want to use Agena on a removable drive or do not have admin rights to run the binary
Windows installer, just install this portable release.

In an NT shell (cmd.exe), create a folder named `agena` anywhere on your drive, change into this
folder and decompress this ZIP file into it, preserving the subdirectory structure of the ZIP file,
which should now look like this (dates and file sizes may vary):

04/10/2026  10:41    <DIR>          bin
29/09/2026  13:01         1,260,722 change.log
03/10/2026  19:04    <DIR>          data
03/10/2026  19:04    <DIR>          doc
03/10/2026  19:15    <DIR>          lib
28/06/2026  11:54             2,118 licence
02/09/2023  08:13             1,588 readme.w64
30/07/2026  10:07               993 run.bat     <-- start-up batch file
03/10/2026  16:29            15,872 run.exe     <-- alternative launcher
03/10/2026  19:04    <DIR>          share       <-- includes icons

Then create a desktop shortcut to the batch file `run.bat` or the binary launcher `run.exe` that
reside at the root of the installation. Choose an icon located in the `share\icons` folder to
beautify the shortcut. Recommendation: choose `agena256.ico`.

Check the properties of the shortcut to be sure that the value in field "Start in" is the
path to the root Agena folder, e.g. `C:\agena`, and not to `C:\agena\bin` or anything else.

This 64-bit Windows edition works fully on Windows 10 and 11. On Windows 8.1 you cannot use the
`gdi` package, but otherwise Agena runs flawlessly there, too. Windows 8 and earlier are not 
supported.

That's it. Have fun !